'''Titi''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that was implemented in [[Version 3.8 Update|Version 3.8]] and can be unlocked as a Stamp Reward during the [[Merc Storia Collaboration Event]]. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 6.2 Update|Version 6.2]] gives her better attack rate and multi-hit.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 191
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Titi
|name2 = Titi CC
|name3 = Titi Cat CC
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Titi CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Titi Cat CC''' when obtained from [[Titi Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage).

==Strategy/Usage==
Titi can be used as a debuffer for any trait; however, she only has Single Target and a mere 20% chance to [[Slow|slow]], so she should not be relied on. She falls short mid-game due to low range and health. However, you can use her to slow short-ranged enemies such as the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s and [[Bore]], though she gets outperformed by trait specific Rare Cats: [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Witch]] for Red, [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop]] for Floating and so on.

Do keep in mind that she can slow all non-Metals, including [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]]. Most enemies that she outranges will fall prey to her slow. However, she is not recommended for peon-heavy stages or stages where there are enemies that have more than 260 range. So, think of Titi as [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer]]'s Normal Form with slow instead of freeze, with a lower chance but more uptime.

==='''True Form'''===
In True Form, she gets multi-hit, slightly shorter attack rate and slightly more damage. The attack power and shortened attack rate are negligible, but the multi-hit essentially boosts her chance to slow. Now, she is safer to use. However, since her range isn't boosted and her health is still too low to survive hits, the original weaknesses still apply.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller}}

